  "slug": "decoding-codes-88bf",
  "summary": "SCOPE reports 173.8 ns latency on a BB code as BP variants, GPU decoders and MWPM speedups target real-time qLDPC and surface-code decoding.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is decoding under real-time constraints, increasingly for qLDPC codes rather than only surface codes. SCOPE, a physics-informed parallel decoder, reports a logical error rate of 4.82e-10 on the [[144,12,12]] bivariate bicycle code with 173.8 ns latency. TEMPO-BP adapts per-variable memory strength via local feedback and lowers failure rates relative to BP+OSD and Relay-BP. Pêlagos scales Relay-BP across multiple GPUs. TCBP-JOBS learns calibrated fault probabilities and matches Tesseract accuracy. A hybrid sliding-window scheme for trapped-ion noise uses soft-output confidence to switch windows and outperforms BP-LSD. For surface codes, Beyond Blossom accelerates CPU MWPM with local predecoding, reporting a 4.23x geometric-mean speedup. A survey frames these efforts as decoder- and code-level hierarchies. Adjacent hardware and design work characterizes temporally correlated leakage in 7x7 surface-code stability experiments on a 105-qubit processor and demonstrates magic state cultivation on IBM devices. A separate study selects rectangular surface-code geometries under biased circuit-level noise to reduce qubit overhead.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
